      "description": "Ashcombe growers and Siltmere reed-cutters bound by mutual aid, but divided over whether the old short route should be reopened. Some trust the colored seedlings as evidence; others see them as a dangerous excuse to claim water and land.",
      "location_ids": [
        "loc_ashcombe",
        "loc_siltmere"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "rul_seasons",
      "statement": "The valley follows ordinary seasons, and the first hard frost ends planting for the year.",
      "category": "physics"
    },
    {
      "id": "rul_watermarks",
      "statement": "In Siltmere Hollow, seedlings sprouting after rain take on faint colors that correspond to the rainwater's path through the valley; the pattern records flow, not ownership or intent.",
      "category": "metaphysics"
    },
    {
      "id": "rul_handwork",
      "statement": "No powered machinery remains in working use; travel, milling, building, and harvest depend on people, animals, water, and salvaged hand-tools.",
      "category": "technology"
    },
    {
      "id": "rul_seedkeeping",
      "statement": "Seed saved for planting must be dried and sealed before the damp season, or it loses much of its ability to sprout.",
      "category": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": "rul_common_measure",
      "statement": "Grain trades are recognized by all four towns only when both parties witness the measure and mark the amount in a shared ledger.",
      "category": "social"
    }
  ],
  "history": [
    {
      "id": "evt_split_harvest",
      "name": "The Missing Measure",
      "description": "Years ago, a grain shipment meant for Ashcombe arrived at Millford short. Millford blamed a flood; Ashcombe accused the weir stewards of keeping the missing sacks. With no trusted ledger to settle the matter, the towns closed the short branch of the seedway.",
      "era": "Years of the Split Route",
      "location_ids": [
        "loc_millford",
        "loc_ashcombe",
        "loc_frostgate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "evt_silt_records",
      "name": "The First Colored Shoots",
      "description": "After a season of unusual floods, Siltmere children noticed that bands of differently colored seedlings followed the channels left by the rain. Their elders began recording the patterns, though the notes were never accepted as proof in the grain dispute.",
      "era": "Years of the Split Route",
      "location_ids": [
        "loc_siltmere"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "evt_last_gathering",
      "name": "The Abandoned Common",
      "description": "The autumn exchange at Frostgate ended when neither rival group would cross the other's path. The meeting walls remain, and old marks cut into their stones still show where each town once stacked its grain.",
      "era": "The Last Shared Autumn",
      "location_ids": [
        "loc_frostgate"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "conflicts": [
    {
      "id": "cnf_grain_route",
      "name": "The Split Seedway",
      "description": "Millford's reserve could carry the towns through winter, but the council refuses to send grain along a route it cannot audit. Ashcombe and Siltmere need the shipment and reject terms that leave them dependent on Millford's ledger. The caravan must broker a measure both sides will witness before frost closes the pass.",
      "faction_ids": [
        "fac_weir_council",
        "fac_terrace_compact",
        "fac_seedwardens"
      ]
    },
