  "world_id": "wld_ninth_bell_estuary",
  "name": "The Silted Cantons",
  "description": "In the Silted Cantons, an estuary city of drowned lanes and leaning parish towers, fog arrives with the tide and lingers long enough to acquire a reputation. Gas mantles and oil lamps give the streets their wavering light. The city’s storm-bells warn of surges, hidden shoals, and the rare fog that turns familiar water into a maze. Their patterns are guarded lore, cast into each bell’s shape by founders who insist that no two warnings should sound alike. When an apprentice hears a pattern no founder remembers making, the parish orders every bell silenced before the next fog. Yet the sound has already traveled through the pilings, and people along the estuary have begun answering it.",
