      "name": "Ashcombe Bell Foundry",
      "description": "A soot-dark workshop on a stone rise above the tide, where bronze is poured into clay molds and each founder marks a casting with a private notch. The oldest molds are kept sealed, though fresh wet clay sometimes appears on their shelves."
    },
    {
      "id": "loc_parish_of_nine",
      "name": "Parish of Nine Tides",
      "description": "A narrow cathedral whose nine storm-bells hang over a sunken nave. Gas jets warm the bell chamber, but the parish keeps the ropes locked and claims the tower has always held only eight."
    },
    {
      "id": "loc_drowned_exchange",
      "name": "The Drowned Exchange",
      "description": "A market of upper floors and boardwalks built above a flooded counting house. Oil lamps burn in glass cages, and traders pass warnings by tapping their stall posts when fog makes speech carry too far."
    },
    {
      "id": "loc_wickwater_steps",
      "name": "Wickwater Steps",
      "description": "A stairway descending into the estuary, its lower landings submerged except at the lowest ebb. The stone is scored with old tally marks that shift in number between tides."
    },
